# B0: the BUILD-ONLY job of the window, run BEFORE A0 while production still serves. C2_ACTIONS=build opens no card, resets nothing and stops nothing: it makes
# the one image of the window (the thin tt-vllm layer over the P8 base, with the traced carry copies in verifier_engine_tp and the tpub smoke rules) from the pushed
# tp4/tpub commit the window sits on. Without it every card job below would fail at its docker run with production already down.
# THE TAG MUST BE FRESH. The build step skips a tag that already exists on the host, so a reused tag would silently serve an old image: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1 is a
# PLACEHOLDER and the driver substitutes ONE new tag, never used before, in every template of this window after checking the tag is absent from the host images.
# Pass: the build log ends with the image tagged, the closure and provenance checks of the build pass. Stop rule: any failure stops the window before production is touched.
# Duration (estimate): 18 min typical, 90 at worst (the first build after a base change).
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card tp4/tpub window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/tpub and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image a build-only job (C2_ACTIONS=build, no card opened) builds from this branch while
# production serves; a later commit of scripts needs a new build and tag. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1 is a PLACEHOLDER the driver may substitute.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-tpub-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
